LAYER-LAW NOTE (binding, discovered on disk)
--------------------------------------------
scripts/simpurity (ADR-017 sim-purity gate) FORBIDS internal/game/** importing
internal/render (bannedImport -> hasPathSegment(p, "render")). Verified by probe:
  internal/game/ui: internal/game/ui/probe.go:3: rendering imports ".../internal/render"
  simpurity: 1 violation(s) in internal/game
So internal/game/ui is presentation-only as the layer law intended, but it CANNOT
blit. Resolution: the package computes geometry and EMITS PanelBox draw commands
through a PanelSink interface; the engine-side painter replays them. The tests
implement PanelSink twice — a recording sink for order/geometry and a painting
sink that replays through render.Surface.DrawDirect into a real 640x480 index
buffer — so the "index-buffer level, not RGBA" AC is met without the layer
importing render outside _test.go (simpurity exempts _test.go by design).

